WEBVTT

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:08.030
<i>Even when twilight arrives
and the darkness swallows all,</i>

00:00:08.030 --> 00:00:15.870
<i>may the ever-twinkling stars in
my heart burn like the morning sun!</i>

00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:42.000
<i>Even if there is an astonishing
amount of anger seething</i>

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:48.470
<i>where their unyielding eyes are focused,</i>

00:00:48.470 --> 00:00:54.910
<i>people will always be able
to stand up, again and again,</i>

00:00:54.910 --> 00:01:01.020
<i>using the lives they were given to their fullest</i>

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:07.330
<i>The hot flames burning in the palms of my hands</i>

00:01:07.330 --> 00:01:14.830
<i>are a strength that everyone
has deep down inside them</i>

00:01:14.830 --> 00:01:18.470
<i>If instead of wavering about the distant future</i>

00:01:18.470 --> 00:01:24.880
<i>you break down the realities
in front of you now one by one</i>

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:28.310
<i>they'll change into ordinary sand</i>

00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:35.120
<i>We can't be worried about appearances</i>

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:39.390
<i>Let's break in through the front gate</i>

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:41.380
<i>Front breaking</i>

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:49.130
<i>Our encounter with a mysterious
puny animal named Pokota</i>

00:01:49.130 --> 00:01:52.140
<i>dragged me, Lina Inverse, and
my self-appointed guardian Gourry</i>

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:53.470
<i>into some strange incidents!</i>

00:01:53.470 --> 00:01:56.710
<i>He claims he was trying to save
Taforashia, a city shrouded in mystery,</i>

00:01:56.710 --> 00:01:59.550
<i>so why did he frame me for crimes he committed?!</i>

00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:02.480
<i>Plus, my arrest warrant was for
the crime of being Lina Inverse!</i>

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:06.390
<i>Some shady assassin and
even a rich old hag tried to kill me,</i>

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:10.320
<i>and then, to top it all off, the legendary
demon beast Zanaffar was revived!</i>

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:12.390
<i>Seriously, enough is enough!</i>

00:02:12.390 --> 00:02:13.660
<i>However...!</i>

00:02:13.660 --> 00:02:19.600
<i>For Lina Inverse, legendary beasts
are no sweat at all, piece o' cake!</i>

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:23.200
<i>Or so I thought, but plenty of
unanswered questions still abound.</i>

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:25.830
<i>Who knows what's going to happen next!</i>

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:29.660
<i>"Newcomer?
A New Journey!"</i>

00:03:12.220 --> 00:03:15.620
That goes like this, and...

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:20.630
Ms. Lina!

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:25.430
It looks like these are the last of
the sorcery books about magical items.

00:03:25.430 --> 00:03:27.260
Yeah? Thanks.

00:03:32.670 --> 00:03:35.440
Amelia! What's the big idea?!

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:37.840
S-Sorry!

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:38.830
Sheesh.

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:44.520
So, did you figure anything out?

00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:46.450
Nope, nothin'...

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:50.020
I guess it's not going to be that easy to find

00:03:50.020 --> 00:03:52.960
any clues about the jar Ozzel spoke of.

00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:54.150
Yeah...

00:03:55.490 --> 00:03:58.500
I want you to find and destroy the jar

00:03:58.500 --> 00:04:02.870
in which the spirit of Red Priest Rezo sleeps.

00:04:02.870 --> 00:04:05.860
The jar in which
Red Priest Rezo's spirit sleeps...

00:04:07.870 --> 00:04:09.710
Red Priest Rezo...

00:04:09.710 --> 00:04:13.140
A blind sorcerer who was
known as a legendary sage...

00:04:15.550 --> 00:04:18.980
Using his matchless magical
power and abundant knowledge,

00:04:18.980 --> 00:04:20.980
he saved countless people...

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:25.160
And when a plague struck Taforashia,

00:04:25.160 --> 00:04:28.060
he put everyone to sleep and sealed them away.

00:04:28.060 --> 00:04:30.050
I owe him my life!

00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:38.400
<i>But, in truth, his one and only
care was to heal his eyes...</i>

00:04:51.850 --> 00:04:54.850
<i>And in the process of opening his blind eyes,</i>

00:04:54.850 --> 00:04:59.830
<i>he wound up reviving the Dark Lord
and destroying himself instead.</i>

00:04:59.830 --> 00:05:04.700
And a jar with Rezo's spirit
is somewhere in this world...

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:08.870
Yeah. So I have to look for it.

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:12.700
To break the seal on my hometown of Taforashia!

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:14.100
Makes sense!

00:05:17.180 --> 00:05:19.610
Let's just hope it's that simple.

00:05:19.610 --> 00:05:21.080
What do you mean?

00:05:21.080 --> 00:05:24.280
There are still tons of unanswered questions.

00:05:24.280 --> 00:05:28.920
Why did Ozzel want us to destroy
this jar with Rezo's spirit in it?

00:05:28.920 --> 00:05:33.060
Not to mention, just who <i>was</i> Ozzel anyway?

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:35.630
What connection did she have with Rezo?

00:05:35.630 --> 00:05:38.130
And one other thing...

00:05:38.130 --> 00:05:41.700
Xellos' involvement in the whole incident.

00:05:41.700 --> 00:05:44.240
At first I thought he had
something to do with the Zanaffar,

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:47.570
but in the end it looks like he didn't.

00:05:47.570 --> 00:05:51.580
That "it's a secret!" guy?

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:53.910
He's not the type to act without a reason.

00:05:53.910 --> 00:05:57.080
Given the fact he <i>has</i> taken action,
he must be up to something.

00:05:57.080 --> 00:06:00.920
Something big enough for
him to neglect a Zanaffar...

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:05.760
Wait, so things could get even
worse than the Zanaffar incident?!

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:07.750
Maybe, if we aren't
careful how we handle things.

00:06:42.630 --> 00:06:46.030
Pardon the intrusion. I've brought your meal.

00:06:52.870 --> 00:06:54.860
How are you feeling?

00:07:02.150 --> 00:07:04.380
But man, a jar...

00:07:04.380 --> 00:07:07.390
Not even the Seyruun
Sorcerers Guild's Great Library

00:07:07.390 --> 00:07:09.820
seemed to have any clues about it...

00:07:09.820 --> 00:07:12.190
How and where are we supposed to find it?

00:07:12.190 --> 00:07:15.180
The only jar that I can recall is...

00:07:20.970 --> 00:07:23.300
Cast off the shackles of your flesh

00:07:23.300 --> 00:07:26.700
and give your spirit unto a transient vessel.

00:07:32.840 --> 00:07:38.840
...that jar he used when we
changed into these bodies...

00:07:41.850 --> 00:07:43.320
Is something wrong?

00:07:43.320 --> 00:07:44.360
Ouch!

00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:46.320
You dimwit!

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:48.830
- What are you doing?!
- What I want!

00:07:48.830 --> 00:07:53.060
That's the jar we're looking for!

00:07:53.060 --> 00:07:54.700
Sheesh...

00:07:54.700 --> 00:07:59.740
Honestly, using a Sword of Light
must really suck away your intelligence!

00:07:59.740 --> 00:08:02.410
Oh, you're too kind!

00:08:02.410 --> 00:08:03.280
Ouch!

00:08:03.280 --> 00:08:05.210
He wasn't complimenting you!

00:08:05.210 --> 00:08:07.040
Huh? He wasn't?

00:08:09.950 --> 00:08:13.390
We haven't seen anyone at all for a while now...

00:08:13.390 --> 00:08:18.890
Well, the Zanaffar <i>did</i> cause major
damage throughout this province.

00:08:18.890 --> 00:08:21.460
So, going back to our discussion earlier,

00:08:21.460 --> 00:08:27.100
one jar can hold and
transfer one person's spirit?

00:08:27.100 --> 00:08:31.770
Yeah. Rezo called them "Hellmaster's Jars."

00:08:31.770 --> 00:08:34.600
Hellmaster? As in Hellmaster Phibrizzo?

00:08:40.980 --> 00:08:44.920
It <i>is</i> a suitable name for something
that can store people's souls...

00:08:44.920 --> 00:08:49.250
So maybe Rezo set things up so
that if something happened to him,

00:08:49.250 --> 00:08:54.060
his spirit would be
transferred to one of those jars?

00:08:54.060 --> 00:08:57.260
I see. So that's what happened...

00:08:57.260 --> 00:09:02.260
- So, where do they sell these jars?
- They don't!

00:09:03.170 --> 00:09:06.300
The only option for now is to try digging up

00:09:06.300 --> 00:09:10.840
any place in Gioconda's
castle that could be related.

00:09:10.840 --> 00:09:12.240
I have to?!

00:09:12.240 --> 00:09:14.480
No complaining! Work your arms off!

00:09:14.480 --> 00:09:19.110
I'm not cut out for manual labor like this!

00:09:21.490 --> 00:09:24.420
Are we really gonna find
the jar in a place like this?!

00:09:24.420 --> 00:09:28.930
I told you, our only option is
to check places one by one!

00:09:28.930 --> 00:09:31.960
Pokota's hometown of Taforashia is sealed away,

00:09:31.960 --> 00:09:33.950
so we start with this place first.

00:09:46.810 --> 00:09:48.180
- Here!
- Right!

00:09:48.180 --> 00:09:49.810
Visfan Rank!

00:09:56.150 --> 00:09:57.780
Found something!

00:10:03.500 --> 00:10:04.860
Isn't this?

00:10:04.860 --> 00:10:06.850
It should lead to the underground lab.

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:12.990
No question about it! Duclis was here!

00:10:21.480 --> 00:10:25.150
It looks like they were conducting
some rather high-level research...

00:10:25.150 --> 00:10:28.420
They <i>were</i> using research
materials stolen from Taforashia.

00:10:28.420 --> 00:10:33.860
Meaning it's possible they
took the Hellmaster's Jar, too.

00:10:33.860 --> 00:10:38.530
They used these to produce
high-level chimeras to use as catalysts...

00:10:38.530 --> 00:10:39.660
Which would mean...

00:10:39.660 --> 00:10:40.570
Come on, now.

00:10:40.570 --> 00:10:46.170
I understand how you feel, but
we're here to find the Hellmaster's Jar.

00:10:46.170 --> 00:10:47.760
Yeah. I know.

00:11:03.890 --> 00:11:05.290
- Gourry!
- Right!

00:11:11.630 --> 00:11:12.620
Bingo!

00:11:18.240 --> 00:11:20.640
I never would've imagined there was more here...

00:11:20.640 --> 00:11:23.140
Were they trying to hide something?

00:11:23.140 --> 00:11:25.130
Or did they seal something away?

00:11:28.580 --> 00:11:30.980
Shh! I hear something!

00:11:38.920 --> 00:11:40.320
Singing?

00:11:43.430 --> 00:11:45.930
Now, I wonder what kind
of devil might lie in our path!

00:11:45.930 --> 00:11:47.760
A singing devil?!

00:11:49.470 --> 00:11:52.070
This way!

00:11:52.070 --> 00:11:57.610
- It's beautiful singing, though!
- Beautiful roses have thorns! Just like me!

00:11:57.610 --> 00:11:59.280
Hey! What's with that reaction?!

00:11:59.280 --> 00:12:03.350
- Ms. Lina! Up ahead!
- Sounds like it's coming from there!

00:12:03.350 --> 00:12:04.980
- Let's go!
- Yeah!

00:12:24.100 --> 00:12:27.310
- These are...
...suits of armor...

00:12:27.310 --> 00:12:30.440
Huh? There's an armor
storeroom in a place like this?

00:12:30.440 --> 00:12:31.840
Shh!

00:12:41.320 --> 00:12:42.950
This suit of armor...

00:12:53.030 --> 00:12:56.470
There you are, monster! Sudden Blam Gush!

00:12:59.000 --> 00:13:02.040
- H-Hey, now, Lina...
- Whoops...

00:13:02.040 --> 00:13:05.510
It could've been some sort of
clue about the Hellmaster's Jar!

00:13:05.510 --> 00:13:07.380
What were you thinking?!

00:13:07.380 --> 00:13:11.720
l-It was some kind of conditioned reflex,
I didn't mean to!

00:13:11.720 --> 00:13:13.150
Conditioned reflex?

00:13:13.150 --> 00:13:15.420
It looks like it's empty.

00:13:15.420 --> 00:13:17.090
Huh?

00:13:17.090 --> 00:13:21.690
Huh? Wasn't the singing coming
from that suit of armor, though?

00:13:21.690 --> 00:13:24.600
- That's how it seemed, but...
- But see for yourself.

00:13:24.600 --> 00:13:26.200
How can that be?

00:13:26.200 --> 00:13:29.190
That's weird.
I definitely felt some resistance...

00:13:32.240 --> 00:13:34.230
- Th-The armor!
- It's floating!

00:13:39.680 --> 00:13:42.710
Hey, you! What's the big idea?!

00:13:42.710 --> 00:13:46.080
- l-It can talk!
- Wh-What's going on?!

00:13:46.080 --> 00:13:51.090
That hurts! You've made me angry! Mad, mad!

00:13:51.090 --> 00:13:54.690
- "Mad, mad"?
- Wh-What is this?

00:13:54.690 --> 00:13:56.290
A suit of Living Armor?

00:13:56.290 --> 00:13:58.430
- Did anything get bent?
- Living Armor?!

00:13:58.430 --> 00:14:01.370
- Uhh, what's that?
- There!

00:14:01.370 --> 00:14:03.070
Living Armor...

00:14:03.070 --> 00:14:08.370
Armor that is given life somehow
and can move around of its own will.

00:14:08.370 --> 00:14:11.410
- Given life somehow?
- Oh, the dust collects so easily...

00:14:11.410 --> 00:14:14.410
Like with the Hellmaster's Jar?!

00:14:14.410 --> 00:14:16.580
A-All right, you!

00:14:16.580 --> 00:14:20.120
I have no desire to talk with
someone who suddenly does painful things!

00:14:20.120 --> 00:14:21.120
Mad, mad!

00:14:21.120 --> 00:14:23.450
l-It looks like she's mad, Ms. Lina!

00:14:23.450 --> 00:14:26.460
Listen! Anyone would bust
out an attack spell or two

00:14:26.460 --> 00:14:31.230
if they ran into suspicious suit
of armor that sings and laughs!

00:14:31.230 --> 00:14:32.430
Hmph!

00:14:32.430 --> 00:14:34.270
You're so not cute!

00:14:34.270 --> 00:14:37.100
Really? I think she's pretty cute myself.

00:14:37.100 --> 00:14:37.740
Huh?!

00:14:37.740 --> 00:14:41.770
All right, all right.
We're the ones at fault for attacking.

00:14:41.770 --> 00:14:46.110
So please talk to us. Who are you?

00:14:46.110 --> 00:14:47.100
Who?

00:14:49.810 --> 00:14:51.850
Yes, who <i>is</i> Nama?!

00:14:51.850 --> 00:14:54.120
That's what <i>we're</i> asking!

00:14:54.120 --> 00:14:57.820
Anyway, I take it your name is Nama?

00:14:57.820 --> 00:15:04.300
Na? I don't know. It might be,
or not, I'm not really sure...

00:15:04.300 --> 00:15:08.800
Your name doesn't matter.
Do you know anything about the jar?

00:15:08.800 --> 00:15:13.140
Jar? Hmm...

00:15:13.140 --> 00:15:15.710
Anything at all! Do you know anything about it?!

00:15:15.710 --> 00:15:18.780
Let's see...

00:15:18.780 --> 00:15:20.140
Oh! The jar!

00:15:20.140 --> 00:15:21.150
You remember?!

00:15:21.150 --> 00:15:26.480
I do! I was searching for treasure!

00:15:26.480 --> 00:15:27.880
Treasure!

00:15:31.190 --> 00:15:35.530
I passed out after that, and when I came to,
I was singing a song here!

00:15:35.530 --> 00:15:37.230
What's with the singing anyway?!

00:15:37.230 --> 00:15:40.300
It's lonely being all by myself!

00:15:40.300 --> 00:15:41.300
Is that how it is?

00:15:41.300 --> 00:15:45.870
In any case, this means that you
haven't always been Living Armor;

00:15:45.870 --> 00:15:48.570
you used to be a normal person, right?

00:15:48.570 --> 00:15:50.170
Normal, huh...

00:15:50.170 --> 00:15:53.180
I could swear I've heard
that voice somewhere before

00:15:53.180 --> 00:15:55.250
and that I don't want to remember where...

00:15:55.250 --> 00:15:56.680
What's wrong?

00:15:56.680 --> 00:16:01.850
I swear I recognize Nama's voice from...
But it couldn't be...

00:16:01.850 --> 00:16:04.560
Huh?! You know her?!

00:16:04.560 --> 00:16:08.690
No, the voice is similar,
but they talk nothing alike...

00:16:08.690 --> 00:16:13.330
Oh, her voice? Well, I'm sure there
are many people with similar voices.

00:16:13.330 --> 00:16:18.400
And who knows, maybe it's Ms. Nama's
parents or siblings you know!

00:16:18.400 --> 00:16:20.440
Parents and siblings, huh...

00:16:20.440 --> 00:16:24.840
Though I'd love to see what the
family of a suit of armor looks like!

00:16:24.840 --> 00:16:26.910
Yeah...

00:16:26.910 --> 00:16:29.880
You appear to be suffering from impaired memory.

00:16:29.880 --> 00:16:32.520
I don't know if it was caused
by the Hellmaster's Jar, though.

00:16:32.520 --> 00:16:36.720
Wh-Where did you find that jar?!
Was it in the tunnels down here?!

00:16:36.720 --> 00:16:41.730
Where? Let me think...

00:16:41.730 --> 00:16:43.900
What a pain in the butt!

00:16:43.900 --> 00:16:46.400
Just remember already!

00:16:46.400 --> 00:16:47.800
M-Ms. Lina!

00:16:47.800 --> 00:16:51.790
For some reason, my conditioned
reflexes spring into action around her...

00:16:56.270 --> 00:16:58.240
Sh-She's acting odd!

00:16:58.240 --> 00:17:02.950
Hitting me in the head with a slipper...
Now you've gone too far!

00:17:02.950 --> 00:17:05.820
Now I'm not gonna tell you <i>anything!</i>

00:17:05.820 --> 00:17:07.790
H-Hey! Apologize!

00:17:07.790 --> 00:17:10.760
Ms. Lina! We might finally have a clue!

00:17:10.760 --> 00:17:14.760
Yes, if she bows down and
puts her head to the ground

00:17:14.760 --> 00:17:18.760
and says, "I'm sorry,
I'll never hit you or defy you again,"

00:17:18.760 --> 00:17:22.430
then maybe I'll reconsider
telling you what you want to know...

00:17:22.430 --> 00:17:24.340
Wh-What?!

00:17:24.340 --> 00:17:26.800
But you don't have to take me up on my offer.

00:17:26.800 --> 00:17:30.270
If you want to wander aimlessly
in search of the jar, be my guest!

00:17:30.270 --> 00:17:33.980
- Hey, Lina!
- Be mature this once, okay?

00:17:33.980 --> 00:17:36.810
As if I'd ever bow to this teapot head!

00:17:36.810 --> 00:17:41.490
T-Teapot head?! I refuse to sit
by quietly as you call me that!

00:17:41.490 --> 00:17:43.590
I'll have to shut you up by force!

00:17:43.590 --> 00:17:48.290
Just you try it! I'll make <i>you</i>
tell us where the jar is by force!

00:17:48.290 --> 00:17:52.630
That's assuming you actually
remember where it was, of course...

00:17:52.630 --> 00:17:53.530
Eep...

00:17:53.530 --> 00:17:56.330
O-Of course I remember where!

00:17:56.330 --> 00:17:59.330
All right, a fight it is! Let's take it outside!

00:18:01.670 --> 00:18:03.510
Talk about convenient...

00:18:03.510 --> 00:18:05.500
You impertinent little!

00:18:06.810 --> 00:18:10.450
This is your last chance to apologize!

00:18:10.450 --> 00:18:13.350
No, this is <i>your</i> last chance
to tell us where the jar is!

00:18:13.350 --> 00:18:15.720
H-Hey, shouldn't we stop them?

00:18:15.720 --> 00:18:19.620
Nah, there's really no stopping
Lina when she gets like that...

00:18:19.620 --> 00:18:23.060
But why is Lina so uptight with Nama?

00:18:23.060 --> 00:18:26.330
Good question. Maybe it's in their chemistry?

00:18:26.330 --> 00:18:29.160
I just hope neither one gets hurt...

00:18:36.370 --> 00:18:40.370
<i>I'll</i> start things off! Flare Arrow!

00:18:47.820 --> 00:18:50.520
That's so weak it's not even worth dodging!

00:18:50.520 --> 00:18:52.820
Curse you and your freakiness!

00:18:52.820 --> 00:18:54.690
Now it's my turn!

00:18:54.690 --> 00:18:56.520
Freeze Arrow!

00:18:57.700 --> 00:18:59.360
Sh-She can use spells too?!

00:18:59.360 --> 00:19:02.830
This is as easy as pie! Freeze Arrow!

00:19:02.830 --> 00:19:04.660
Flare Arrow!

00:19:06.940 --> 00:19:07.610
Huh?

00:19:07.610 --> 00:19:09.410
Gotcha!

00:19:09.410 --> 00:19:11.240
Freeze Arrow!

00:19:14.080 --> 00:19:15.780
This is insane!

00:19:15.780 --> 00:19:16.750
Why, you!

00:19:16.750 --> 00:19:22.520
Yes, running around like a
headless chicken suits you very well!

00:19:22.520 --> 00:19:23.050
Why, you!

00:19:23.050 --> 00:19:26.020
Still, she'll probably recover
from a regular-level spell right away,

00:19:26.020 --> 00:19:28.790
so in one sense, she's even
more of a pain than the Zanaffar!

00:19:28.790 --> 00:19:31.960
Now, why don't you give it up?

00:19:31.960 --> 00:19:36.070
If you don't come out, then
I'll just wipe out everything!

00:19:36.070 --> 00:19:39.970
Supreme King with the frozen soul!
Grant me the power of your icy rage...!

00:19:39.970 --> 00:19:42.960
I'll beat you to that major spell! Digger Bolt!

00:19:45.540 --> 00:19:47.780
Hah! That spell won't work on me!

00:19:47.780 --> 00:19:50.210
Now it's my turn! Dynast Bras...!

00:19:52.080 --> 00:19:54.890
What is this?!

00:19:54.890 --> 00:19:57.890
How does it feel to be a jury-rigged magnet?

00:19:57.890 --> 00:19:59.590
M-Magnet?!

00:19:59.590 --> 00:20:05.760
That's right! That lightning bolt
turned your metal body into a magnet!

00:20:05.760 --> 00:20:08.500
That phony body of yours worked against you!

00:20:08.500 --> 00:20:14.910
Now to melt this scrap metal
and turn it into a real teapot!

00:20:14.910 --> 00:20:18.440
Darkness beyond twilight,
crimson beyond blood that flows!

00:20:18.440 --> 00:20:21.780
Buried in the flow of time, in thy great name

00:20:21.780 --> 00:20:24.450
I pledge myself to darkness!

00:20:24.450 --> 00:20:25.850
Run!

00:20:25.850 --> 00:20:28.990
- She always has to be so reckless!
- Then stop her!

00:20:28.990 --> 00:20:32.920
All the fools who stand in
our way shall be destroyed

00:20:32.920 --> 00:20:38.700
by the power you and I possess!

00:20:38.700 --> 00:20:40.100
I don't wanna be a teapot!

00:20:40.100 --> 00:20:43.090
Dragon Slave!

00:20:53.940 --> 00:20:55.650
She did it...

00:20:55.650 --> 00:20:57.820
There goes our big clue...

00:20:57.820 --> 00:20:59.810
There was nothing we could do.

00:21:01.820 --> 00:21:03.990
What's the big idea?

00:21:03.990 --> 00:21:06.190
Geez, you're stubborn!

00:21:06.190 --> 00:21:08.490
What's it gonna be? Still wanna fight?

00:21:08.490 --> 00:21:08.990
No, no!

00:21:08.990 --> 00:21:12.030
Oh! I just remembered where the jar is!

00:21:12.030 --> 00:21:13.230
I hope that's the truth.

00:21:13.230 --> 00:21:16.830
If you're just saying that,
I really <i>will</i> turn you into a teapot!

00:21:16.830 --> 00:21:18.200
It's the truth!

00:21:18.200 --> 00:21:21.640
So, please! Anything but a teapot!

00:21:26.680 --> 00:21:30.510
Just be patient for a little longer...

00:21:30.510 --> 00:21:33.050
...Until your new arms set in.

00:21:33.050 --> 00:21:34.820
Lina...

00:21:34.820 --> 00:21:38.090
Find out what Lina Inverse is up to...

00:21:38.090 --> 00:21:39.690
Understood.

00:21:39.690 --> 00:21:42.890
I will... I will accept a number of jobs.

00:21:42.890 --> 00:21:49.890
As a way to test out these arms...
Any jobs at all... From anyone...

00:21:57.840 --> 00:22:05.220
<i>What can save this grieving heart?</i>

00:22:05.220 --> 00:22:08.720
<i>I've driven myself into a corner</i>

00:22:08.720 --> 00:22:16.960
<i>and am steeped in my own broken tears</i>

00:22:16.960 --> 00:22:24.400
<i>I know how not to give up</i>

00:22:24.400 --> 00:22:31.410
<i>I believe in the path I've chosen</i>

00:22:31.410 --> 00:22:44.760
<i>Even so, what if I come
across pain that won't go away?</i>

00:22:44.760 --> 00:22:51.930
<i>I want to be strong always,</i>

00:22:51.930 --> 00:23:01.170
<i>so that I can take in your sadness</i>

00:23:01.170 --> 00:23:08.510
<i>Even the meaning of my continued
life has been called into question</i>

00:23:08.510 --> 00:23:11.980
<i>I have no answer at all to give</i>

00:23:11.980 --> 00:23:18.620
<i>I'm simply going to walk forward with my head up</i>

00:23:22.160 --> 00:23:25.800
<i>We're looking for the Hellmaster's Jar,
so what's the deal with Nama?!</i>

00:23:25.800 --> 00:23:29.030
<i>Huh? Another suit of armor?
This one's a headless dulluhan?</i>

00:23:29.030 --> 00:23:31.300
<i>On the next Slayers Evolution-R:</i>

00:23:31.300 --> 00:23:33.170
<i>"Oh My Head!
Where's My Head?"</i>

00:23:33.170 --> 00:23:36.000
<i>If you don't watch, I'll go berserk!</i>
